The term “Driver’s License” shall refer to:

(a) A license, issued by the State of Mayflower, that permits an individual to drive on public roads.

The term “Commercial Driver’s License” and “CDL” shall refer to:

(a) A license, issued by the State of Mayflower, permits an individual to drive vehicles classified as ‘Commercial Vehicles’.

No person shall be able to operate a motor vehicle on public roads without a valid driver’s license issued by the State of Mayflower.

No person shall be able to operate a commercial vehicle on public roads without a valid commercial driver’s license issued by the State of Mayflower.

Law Enforcement shall have the authority to suspend a driver’s license or CDL for a given period of time when issuing an infraction for a violation of the vehicle code.

Any individual who is in violation of the shall be eligible for suspension of their driver’s license or CDL:

(a) Any degree of Reckless driving;

(b) 2 M.S.C. § 1215 "Excessive Speeding";

(c) 2 M.S.C. § 1211 "Obstruction of Traffic";

(d) 1 M.S.C. § 1505 "Failure to Pay a Citation";

(e) 1 M.S.C. § 1701 "Import of Prohibited Goods";

(f) 1 M.S.C. § 1409 "Smuggling."

(g) Any crime under Title 1, Subtitle 1, Chapter VII of the Mayflower Criminal Code where the vehicle was utilized in the commission of a crime.

Any individual who also has committed three (3) traffic violations within no more than a twenty-four (24) hour period shall be eligible for suspension of their driver’s license or CDL.

